# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored -- never commit real credentials.
#
# These exact names are required. The copernicusmarine CLI reads them itself, so
# nothing here has to implement authentication; this project only decides what the
# CLI subprocess inherits.
#
# COPERNICUS_USERNAME / COPERNICUS_PASSWORD are silently ignored -- no warning, no
# error. They were wrong in this repo's .env for a while. See `copernicusmarine
# login --help` for the authoritative list.
#
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# An environment variable that is already set always wins over this file, so
#   COPERNICUSMARINE_SERVICE_PASSWORD=... uv run python scripts/load_db.py
# overrides without editing anything. That is also how CI supplies secrets.
#
# Alternative: `copernicusmarine login` (interactive) writes to
# ~/.copernicusmarine/ and works too. .env is here because login cannot be
# scripted and cannot run unattended in a room.
COPERNICUSMARINE_SERVICE_USERNAME=
COPERNICUSMARINE_SERVICE_PASSWORD=
